{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466456-fera-and-genetics","id":1466456,"title":"Fera and genetics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-03T06:45:11-07:00","id":1466456,"title":"Fera and genetics","content":"While described as 'super natural', it seems obvious that whether or not an individual is a Fera is determined by genetics. <br /> <br /> So my question is can Fera be turned into a human or a human turned into a Fera by changing an individuals genetic make-up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26970-blu44","name":"Blu44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T07:57:35-07:00","id":1466462,"title":"","content":"If it is entirely genetic then yes, but I don't think it is entirely genetic at all. Also genetic modification of the Fera has a history of really bad results (see attempts to bring back the Bunyip). If I were going to make this into a storyline, the one thing I wouldn't do is have it go smoothly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T08:31:16-07:00","id":1466466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blu44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466456-fera-and-genetics#post1466456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While described as 'super natural', it seems obvious that whether or not an individual is a Fera is determined by genetics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... I think you might need to expand on this a lot. For example, how do the Ratkin or Corax fit into the idea that this is all genetics?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So my question is can Fera be turned into a human or a human turned into a Fera by changing an individuals genetic make-up? </div> </div> </div>You can't turn a human into kinfolk or Fera by messing with their genes. You can't &quot;revert&quot; kinfolk or Fera through some sort of retroviral editing.<br /> <br /> You probably can genetically tamper with a fetus and destroy the material connections to its supernatural affinity rendering a child that might have been kinfolk or Fera a human (or appropriate animal).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466456-fera-and-genetics?p=1466462#post1466462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIf I were going to make this into a storyline, the one thing I wouldn't do is have it go smoothly.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth looking into the antagonist group Developmental Neogenetics Amalgamated (DNA, ha ha) if you want to look into one of the ways the writers have approached the general concept.<br /> <br /> DNA are a group of human werewolf &quot;hunters&quot; that believe the Fera are a genetic disease that can be cured. While not openly Weaver servants like Pentex works for the Wyrm, DNA is shadow funded by a number of Weaver aligned and Weaver adjacent entities in the WoD. While DNA has shown genetics do matter a lot for the Garou, they have run into a number of stumbling blocks towards a scientific understanding of the condition because it is a mix of supernatural and mundane components. For example, they struggle heavily with trying to explain how shapeshifting wildly violates the laws of physics, and how a genetic disorder could possibly result in that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T17:55:28-07:00","id":1466554,"title":"","content":"Accumulated lore has it that it's spiritual heritage, not genetics. The genetic component is basically just a marker; kin and changer (Fera is a word that Garou use to refer to non-Garou changers) will have the same markers, and be genetically indistinguishable, because there is no protein or group of proteins that can warp physics and cross over into the Umbra, even if Developmental Neogenetics Amalgamated insists otherwise and continues to bang its head against a brick wall trying to prove it (spoilers: they're bound for failure, forever, as long as they cling to their scifi fringe hypotheses).<br /> <br /> Lore also has it that if you clone a Garou or Fera, you get either kinfolk (if homid or born of an animal) or a stillborn corpse (if born of two of the same kind of changer, where applicable). Bringing to term the result of a Garou-Garou union or what have you requires that the mother has Rage and is capable of shapeshifting. This information, incidentally, is in the Revised Storyteller's Handbook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T01:23:44-07:00","id":1466622,"title":"","content":"I agree, that the fact if an individual is garou/fera (for most fera) is supernatural. However, it is hereditary, and geneticists might analyse the DNA of a garou/fera and by finding family traits would be able to detect the garou/fera relatives. Meaning, that kinfolk and other garou/fera could be found in a large number of DNA samples from the general population. Doesn't mean that the test would determine the difference between kinfolk or garou/feta.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T10:32:30-07:00","id":1466675,"title":"","content":"The game is very explicit that Garou (and other Changing Breeds) are half spirit and half flesh. The game is also clear that it is not genes that determine if someone is Garou. In other words, it is the spirit side of Garou that determines things. Therefore no amount of genetic manipulation can create Garou. It is whether the person inherits the spirit component (which is not detectable or manipulable by science).<br /> <br /> Whatever the laws are of &quot;spirit inheritance&quot; is, they are likely completely alien to genetic science.<br /> <br /> To a lot lesser degree, this is probably true of kinfolk as well. While they are not made of spirit, there probably is some kind of spirit force that clings to them that marks them as different and allows them to pass on the spirit ancestry to full fledged Garou (and which sometimes allows kinfolk to have slight supernatural powers themselves).<br /> <br /> Is there wiggle room? Of course there can be. The spirit side, while not part of real world science, could be affected by some kind of super science. The company DNA, whether it is the original version of Garou hunters being secretly supported by the Progenitors or the revised version of some kind of Weaver controlled company, should have some of that. And there are still certain genetic markers in Garou because they are still half flesh, though how that is tied to any supernatural powers is unclear. So if an ST wanted to run a plot along these lines, I think it's OK as long as it is shown that there are special reasons for it that would not be available to the greater public.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T10:57:30-07:00","id":1466680,"title":"","content":"Its also worth of note that genetics also follow a lot of laws that changers willfully ignore. It is completely impossible to have an animal that is able to breed with two species with completely incompatible chromosomal sets, as it impacts gamete and embryo formation.<br /> <br /> And on regards to a full grown being... what do you even mean by changing someone's genes? The genetic code isn't stored in any particular place in the body, it is copied in every single cell and copies may have mutations. To change the entire genetic make-up of someone simply isn't a thing, at least after embryonic stages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T12:34:18-07:00","id":1466695,"title":"","content":"Well, there is 1st Edition and the Garou/Bastet-Hybrid form the &quot;Call to Battle&quot; novel, which never materialized into a series, thank Gaia. But, there was a Progenitor doing the genetic manipulations, so.... it's magick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T15:53:18-07:00","id":1466715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466456-fera-and-genetics?p=1466695#post1466695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there is 1st Edition and the Garou/Bastet-Hybrid form the &quot;Call to Battle&quot; novel, which never materialized into a series, thank Gaia. But, there was a Progenitor doing the genetic manipulations, so.... it's magick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keeping in mind that a changer may also be Kinfolk to other changers.<br /> <br /> One of my wife's fav chars is a Ghural that is closer to the Garou because she's an active Glass Walker kinfolk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-04T19:43:44-07:00","id":1466741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466456-fera-and-genetics?p=1466715#post1466715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keeping in mind that a changer may also be Kinfolk to other changers.<br /> <br /> One of my wife's fav chars is a Ghural that is closer to the Garou because she's an active Glass Walker kinfolk.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's still a whole, discrete Gurahl that happens to be kinfolk to Garou rather than a Garou that is also a Bastet for some reason, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T09:49:56-07:00","id":1466780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466456-fera-and-genetics?p=1466741#post1466741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's still a whole, discrete Gurahl that happens to be kinfolk to Garou rather than a Garou that is also a Bastet for some reason, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's for sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T00:12:09-08:00","id":1467773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466456-fera-and-genetics?p=1466466#post1466466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um... I think you might need to expand on this a lot. For example, how do the Ratkin or Corax fit into the idea that this is all genetics?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There are exemptions to every rule. But most Fera are randomly created through birth. Which means there would be a genetic aspect. Or maybe it is all magic, I don't know. But in my mind, it would seem that there are genetic factors at play.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466456-fera-and-genetics?p=1466466#post1466466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can't turn a human into kinfolk or Fera by messing with their genes. You can't &quot;revert&quot; kinfolk or Fera through some sort of retroviral editing.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>While this was something I was not planning on trying, I am interested in knowing why. Kinfolk just means they are related to a Fera and have the potential of breeding one. If it is not because of genetics, then what is it? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466456-fera-and-genetics?p=1466466#post1466466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You probably can genetically tamper with a fetus and destroy the material connections to its supernatural affinity rendering a child that might have been kinfolk or Fera a human (or appropriate animal).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If it can be done to a fetus, I see no reason it could not be done to an adult, although obviously it would be a lot more complicated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466456-fera-and-genetics?p=1466466#post1466466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's worth looking into the antagonist group Developmental Neogenetics Amalgamated (DNA, ha ha) if you want to look into one of the ways the writers have approached the general concept.<br /> <br /> DNA are a group of human werewolf &quot;hunters&quot; that believe the Fera are a genetic disease that can be cured. While not openly Weaver servants like Pentex works for the Wyrm, DNA is shadow funded by a number of Weaver aligned and Weaver adjacent entities in the WoD. While DNA has shown genetics do matter a lot for the Garou, they have run into a number of stumbling blocks towards a scientific understanding of the condition because it is a mix of supernatural and mundane components. For example, they struggle heavily with trying to explain how shapeshifting wildly violates the laws of physics, and how a genetic disorder could possibly result in that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will look into that. Do you happen to know what book they are in?<br /> <br /> And thanks for your response. Sorry it took me so long to reply, I don't visit this forum very often,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26970-blu44","name":"Blu44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T02:33:28-08:00","id":1467780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blu44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466456-fera-and-genetics?p=1467773#post1467773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are exemptions to every rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the relatively small sample size, exceptions are hard to dismiss as outliers.<br /> <br /> A more general example that applies to more Fera than not: there is no way to explain, with pure genetics, how a person born of two human parents can successfully breed with a non-primate animal. Even within the realms of genetic hybrids, at least in animals, they require very close genetics to have the potential to be viable. There's no way to explain with real world science how a male Bastet born of two human kin could go have sex is a wild female puma and it result in genetically puma offspring.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which means there would be a genetic aspect. Or maybe it is all magic, I don't know. But in my mind, it would seem that there are genetic factors at play. </div> </div> </div>It's both. I'm not sure why that seems to be a sticking point. Yes, there is some level of genetics at play, but there's also enough magic involved that you can't analyze this with just genetic and explain how things work in the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kinfolk just means they are related to a Fera and have the potential of breeding one. </div> </div> </div>It means significantly more than that, even if largely in potential for access to magical abilities that is rare to see happen (such has Kinfolk that have Gnosis, or ones that manage to learn Gifts, things normal humans can't do).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it is not because of genetics, then what is it? </div> </div> </div>The magic side of things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it can be done to a fetus, I see no reason it could not be done to an adult, although obviously it would be a lot more complicated. </div> </div> </div>Because it doesn't follow scientific rules.<br /> <br /> Think of it this way: once the genetic potential to form a spiritual connection is expressed, the spiritual connection kicks in to protect itself from tampering.<br /> <br /> There are ways to break it, but those have to involve the supernatural to overcome a spiritual effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I will look into that. Do you happen to know what book they are in? </div> </div> </div>Book of the Weaver.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T11:33:49-08:00","id":1467805,"title":"","content":"On genetic tampering with adults:<br /> <br /> Genetic expression is an extremely complex phenomenon. The expression of a gene isn't just the result of its presence in your body, but the interaction of the gene with the current make-up of the cell it's in, plus external factors and other genes.<br /> <br /> So while you can have a big impact by genetically tampering with gametes or a zygotic cell, the further development goes the less you can affect the organism through genetic tampering, even if you actually manage to alter it in every cell in the same way.<br /> <br /> In short, even if it was just about genetics, tampering with the genes that make a person Kinfolk or Changer doesn't necessarily have an effect on a grown up, or even on a child. Depending on how the <i>expression</i> of the gene causes the state it can take time or be outright impossible to alter, and be so from any particular point in life starting at early cell differentiation.<br /> <br /> Altering an adult's genetic make-up to resemble a wolf wouldn't result in a werewolf, a wolf hybrid or a wolf transformation. It would result in metabolic collapse. It doesn't have to be this drastic, either, completely changing a small percentage of an adult genetic code to resemble that of another person may also result in catastrophic metabolic collapse. Gene editing is, by all means, rocket science.<br /> <br /> ====================<br /> <br /> On the matter of genetic compatibility for generating offspring.<br /> <br /> The ability of generating offspring derives primarily from chromosomal compatibility. Two gametes can only fuse if they have enough compatibility to have a hard maximum of 1 unpaired chromosome in the resultant cell. This depends on both number of chromosomes and form, as too distinct chromosomes won't pair at all.<br /> <br /> What this means is that only following the laws of genetics it is impossible to have an organism that can breed true with two species too distinct. There is a caveat I'll talk about later. Humans have 23 chromosome pairs, wolves have 39. Even before comparing format it is mathematically impossible to viably pair them.<br /> <br /> Not without &quot;anomalous&quot; help, where comes the caveat. In theory maybe you could have a species that can game this system to force the cross. But how would you do it without magic? And what's the role of the Kinfolk in this situation? This species need to have a bigger genetic code than any of the other two as it must house the distinct genes, and a way to produce viable gametes for both. Since Kinfolk are capable of producing Changers, they all must be able to pass down the whole anomalous code, so Kinfolk couldn't be genetically human, they'd have to be genetically Changer, which brings a huge amount of assumptions and consequences of their own.<br /> <br /> Most importantly, though, it would be noticeable. In a world where Garou exist and follow strictly the laws of genetics, Kinfolk DNA wouldn't pass as anything remotely similar to human. The first time a Lost Kinfolk gets to have not even DNA <i>per se</i>, just their chromosomes under a microscope, it would be enough to blow up the veil royally. That thing would need natural properties that don't exist in any vertebrate, at the very least.<br /> <br /> Since WtA isn't that world, and even the D.N.A. group barely managed to find a couple suspected genetic markers after specifically studying Garou and Kinfolk genetics, we can only conclude that the magical aspects are of considerable importance and maybe completely divorced from genetics (since although closely related, genetics isn't the same thing as hereditary or congenital).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T20:11:43-08:00","id":1467852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blu44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466456-fera-and-genetics?p=1467773#post1467773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are exemptions to every rule. But most Fera are randomly created through birth.</div> </div> </div> </div>We experience it as a rough statistical frequency. That doesn't give us any real idea about what's behind said frequency, which Garou and Fera would generally be inclined to ascribe as Gaia's choice, favor, or other sort of spiritual grace or gift. And that might as well be it, because W:tA doesn't really play or hit the same way if you try to crowbar in alternate explanations; it is best played as literally as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T22:09:11-08:00","id":1467856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466456-fera-and-genetics?p=1467852#post1467852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it is best played as literally as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure, but it does indeed change a lot if you stray too much of its own explanations.<br /> <br /> And when your natural biological properties include fucking with Conservation of Mass and moving inside mirrors, a hard sci-fi take isn't very compatible.<br /> <br /> But personally I actually do like in my games to explore the notion that Kinfolk aren't actually as human as they seem, being just as much another species as the Changers themselves. They just don't look like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T22:49:36-08:00","id":1467857,"title":"","content":"I can't help but feel that a group with a sufficient background in genetics and speciation to appreciate an in depth look at trying to taxonomicly classify kinfolk and Garou would also be a group that would very quickly jump to, &quot;it's magic, move on,&quot; just like any bio-physicists trying to explain the violations of conservation of mass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T04:56:06-08:00","id":1467867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466456-fera-and-genetics?p=1466741#post1466741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's still a whole, discrete Gurahl that happens to be kinfolk to Garou rather than a Garou that is also a Bastet for some reason, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I read somewhere (but I can't remember where) that there's no such thing as Garou-Bastet hybrid. This character will be garou (or bastet) but with special connections to the other race. The thing that wasn't mentioned was what happens to the children of such character. I believe that, if mentioned kid would ever experience first change, its race should be determined randomly. As for werewolf genetics take a look at this document:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.mcdonald.me.uk/storytelling/Werewolf%20Genetics%20Primer.htm\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://www.white-wolf.com/darkspiral/darkspiral.gif\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.mcdonald.me.uk/storytelling/Werewolf%20Genetics%20Primer.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> Untitled Document </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.mcdonald.me.uk/storytelling/Werewolf%20Genetics%20Primer.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.mcdonald.me.uk/storytelling/Werewolf%20Genetics%20Primer.htm </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T05:06:23-08:00","id":1467868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466456-fera-and-genetics?p=1467867#post1467867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read somewhere (but I can't remember where) that there's no such thing as Garou-Bastet hybrid</div> </div> </div> </div>There shouldn't be. Not naturally anyway. In the novel, that was supposed to be a trilogy (according to the cover) the main character was explicitly a person, whom was experimented on by his adoptive father, who was a mage, supposedly of the Progenitor group within the Technocracy - along with the other shifter kids in his military academy / boarding school setup.<br /> <br /> It was some 1st Edition craziness, if I recall correctly. Not to be meant to be canon in the way the games have developed...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T05:26:34-08:00","id":1467871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466456-fera-and-genetics?p=1467868#post1467868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There shouldn't be. Not naturally anyway. In the novel, that was supposed to be a trilogy (according to the cover) the main character was explicitly a person, whom was experimented on by his adoptive father, who was a mage, supposedly of the Progenitor group within the Technocracy - along with the other shifter kids in his military academy / boarding school setup.<br /> <br /> It was some 1st Edition craziness, if I recall correctly. Not to be meant to be canon in the way the games have developed...</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that we talk about the different characters. I recall the character of which you're talking about but without any further details. I was talking about a character from one of the stories from &quot;When will you rage&quot; (I believe that it was &quot;A third world&quot; by Graham Watkins). But basically I agree, there should be no such thing as Garou Bastet hybrid. As I mentioned I read it somewhere, I think it was either storytellers or players guide/handbook. Of course I also think that it is entirely possible p. ex. for a Garou to have a drop of other fera blood in his veins and even some stranger creatures (like a lost child of Danislavs revenant who were also Shadow Lord kinfolks).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 11-15-2021, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T06:10:00-08:00","id":1467875,"title":"","content":"I browsed over the story, and it might be the same character: Jay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T07:00:52-08:00","id":1467879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466456-fera-and-genetics?p=1467875#post1467875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I browsed over the story, and it might be the same character: Jay.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't \ud83d\ude42. I also refreshed my memory and the character I was speaking about is Rhetta Arquel, the granddaughter of Children of Gaia and Balam kinfolk. There's a character named Jay in this story but he works for DNA and tries to capture the girl for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T11:52:09-08:00","id":1467897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466456-fera-and-genetics?p=1467857#post1467857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but feel that a group with a sufficient background in genetics and speciation to appreciate an in depth look at trying to taxonomicly classify kinfolk and Garou would also be a group that would very quickly jump to, &quot;it's magic, move on,&quot; just like any bio-physicists trying to explain the violations of conservation of mass.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think D.N.A. is as prepared as they purport to be for this very reason, although I disagree with the &quot;move on&quot; only in the sense that they would want to study this magic and its interactions with their field.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T14:05:37-08:00","id":1467920,"title":"","content":"The issue is that the whole addition of magic doesn't inform the already intensely debated issue of what a species even is. One of the dirty little secrets of biology is, despite how much is built of the idea of there being a distinct unit of life called a &quot;species,&quot; we have spent centuries trying to come up with a functional definition of one, and we have consistently and utterly failed.<br /> <br /> We have a whole branch of biology that is built off of &quot;move on&quot; from that question and just accept an bodged together &quot;good enough&quot; approach so we can get to all the fascinating science that happens if you take that species are even a thing as an unchallenged premise.<br /> <br /> The reason &quot;move on&quot; is inherently going to happen is because there's three main schools of how to even approach the idea of a species, over two dozen moderately functional models of how to determine what a species is (all of which have strengths and flaws), and nothing in studying Garou genetic-magic breeding does anything more than complicate an already overly complex debate. The Fera just add the unscientific &quot;magic&quot; issue to the classic ring species dilemma.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T23:07:40-08:00","id":1468234,"title":"","content":"When Pentex created Mockery breeds, I think it's implied they're using some Enlightened Hyperscience to do so. Genetics would pay a small part of it, but it's mostly about manipulating the spirit (Through magickal &quot;Science&quot; <br /> If you want to ignore mage, perhaps the best sollution would be to have all the science gear in the lab double as Fetishes which provides them with a magical capability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T00:02:03-08:00","id":1468238,"title":"","content":"Possibly it is &quot;only&quot; hedge magic, but still far from mundane cutting edge science.<br /> <br /> I mean, stuff like Black Hand Bio-Thauma is also closer to Hedge Magic than to true Magick. On the other hand &quot;Masters of the Art&quot; stated creation of a new Changing Breed as something one would need Life 6 arch sphere magick for.... So, whibbely-whobbely-whity-wolfy......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T15:59:37-08:00","id":1468305,"title":"","content":"Weird science inspired and helped by Wyrm's servants and powers is a good enough rationalisation for anything like that. It's a narrative construct that doesn't need to be supported by player facing mechanics. Especially from a different gameline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-18T16:00:01-08:00","id":1468306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466456-fera-and-genetics?p=1468234#post1468234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue anima